ntifying, assessing, and mitigating technological risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential technological pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents technological anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2132, 2133), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 10, 14))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services and Governance\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on regional availability, noted starting Q2 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (2136), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 10, 10))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the SAP Build Process Automation and Cloud Identity Services Departments, established in Q2 2024, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (2132, 2136), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 10, 14))]\n\n## Forms Service by Adobe Operational Scope\n\nThe Forms Service by Adobe Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in ensuring that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on configuration tool updates, noted starting Q1 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (2134), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 10, 11))]\n\n## UI Theme Designer Updates\n\nThe UI Theme Designer Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in ensuring that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on base theming content updates, noted starting Q1 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (2135), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 10, 11))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Cloud Services, focusing on key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's cloud operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Services Operational Scope\n\nSAP Cloud Services play a pivotal role in supporting the company's cloud operations, ensuring compliance with regulatory standards, and managing financial risks effectively. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services and Governance\n\nCloud Identity Services ensure that all SAP's cloud operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (6), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between Cloud Identity Services and other departments ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (8, 9), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Deprecation of Container-Based Applications Pipeline\n\nThe Container-Based Applications pipeline has been deprecated and will be removed from the service on December 31st, 2024. Existing jobs will continue to function until this date. We recommend using the Kyma Runtime pipeline instead. [Data: Source (10), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## New Google Cloud Region for SAP Document AI\n\nSAP Document AI is now available in the Google Cloud region ap30 - Australia (Sydney). This update enhances the company's capabilities in document processing and analysis. [Data: Source (11), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Deprecation of SAP Ariba Category Management connector\n\nEffective August 25, 2025, the SAP Ariba Category Management connector will be deprecated. This change is due to an update of the business solution’s local user store, which no longer requires user provisioning jobs. [Data: Source (14), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]", "# Joule and SAP BTP Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into the key components of Joule and SAP BTP, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide innovative solutions for businesses. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Joule's Operational Scope\n\nJoule plays a pivotal role in providing innovative solutions for businesses. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard businesses against potential technological pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective Joule implementation not only prevents technological anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. Joule is now available in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition for navigational use cases [Data: Sources (2128, 2129), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 10), (2024, 10, 14))].\n\n## SAP BTP's Role in Business Operations\n\nSAP BTP ensures that all business operations adhere to the technological standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on providing innovative solutions, noted starting 2024, is crucial in maintaining businesses' reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technological standards and ethical practices. SAP BTP Developer's Guide has been updated to include a link to the Architecting Multi-Region Resiliency for SAP BTP Use Cases reference architecture [Data: Source (2121), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 15), (2024, 10, 15))].\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between Joule and SAP BTP ensures that innovative solutions are technologically sound and that compliance measures consider business risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating Joule with SAP BTP strategies at businesses. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with technological requirements. Joule booster has been updated to create a Joule formation in the System Landscape in SAP BTP [Data: Sources (2126, 2127), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 14), (2024, 10, 14))].", "# SAP Technology and Services Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technologies and services, highlighting their relationships and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's operations and development around 2024.\n\n## Joule Updates and Availability\n\nJoule, a key SAP technology, has undergone several updates and expansions in 2024. These include new use cases in Cross-Area Capabilities, data center availability, and document grounding capability. Joule's availability and updates are crucial for SAP's customers and developers, enabling them to leverage the technology's capabilities effectively. [Data: Sources (101, 102, 103, 104, 105), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 10), (2024, 10, 14))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation and Integration\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has introduced new features, including Guided Process in Process Editor and SAP Build Process Automation, Foundation Add-On by UiPath. These updates enhance the technology's capabilities, enabling customers to automate processes more efficiently. The integration with UiPath automation capabilities further expands the technology's potential. [Data: Sources (2132, 2133), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 14), (2024, 10, 14))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services and Regional Availability\n\nCloud Identity Services has undergone changes, including regional availability and IP updates. The service now operates with one deployment and two IPs in the Australia/Japan region, which is only for Australia. Customers must update their allowed IP lists to ensure seamless service usage. [Data: Source (2136), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 10), (2024, 10, 10))]\n\n## Peppol Exchange Enhancements\n\nPeppol Exchange has introduced enhancements, including updates to schematron files for A-NZ Peppol BIS Billing, XRechnung, and SI-UBL 2.0. These changes will be active in the production environment as of August 24, 2024. Customers must update their participants and party ID types to ensure continued service usage. [Data: Sources (2361, 2362), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 23), (2024, 08, 24))]\n\n## SAP Digital Payments Add-On and Payment Features\n\nSAP Digital Payments Add-On has introduced new features, including the ability to use pre-registered payment cards or bank accounts and payment type icon URLs. These updates enhance the technology's capabilities, enabling customers to process payments more efficiently. [Data: Sources (2363, 2364), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 23), (2024, 08, 23))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Updates and Improvements\n\nSAP Document AI has undergone updates and improvements, including more accurate date format identification, new improved machine learning models, and document feature enhancements. These changes enhance the technology's capabilities, enabling customers to extract and process documents more efficiently. [Data: Sources (2365, 2366, 2367), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 23), (2024, 09, 09))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Cloud Services, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the company's operations as of 2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nCloud Foundry is a key component of SAP Cloud Services, providing a platform for building, deploying, and managing applications. It supports multiple environments, including Cloud Foundry, Kyma, and Neo. The platform offers a range of features, including automated scaling, load balancing, and security. [Data: Sources (34, 1132), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 31), (2025, 03, 31))]\n\n## SAP BTP and Cloud Services\n\nSAP BTP (Business Technology Platform) is a comprehensive platform that includes Cloud Foundry, Kyma, and Neo. It provides a range of services, including application development, data management, and analytics. The platform is designed to support the company's digital transformation and operational efficiency. [Data: Sources (1133, 3812), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 29), (2025, 03, 31))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services\n\nCloud Identity Services is a critical component of SAP Cloud Services, providing identity and access management capabilities. It supports multiple environments, including Cloud Foundry, Kyma, and Neo. The service offers a range of features, including user authentication, authorization, and single sign-on. [Data: Sources (1136, 3816), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 27), (2025, 03, 31))]", "# Cloud Foundry Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key components and features within the Cloud Foundry technology framework, highlighting their relationships and significance in the context of technology advancements. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Decentralized Identity Verification Capabilities\n\nThe Decentralized Identity Verification component at Cloud Foundry plays a pivotal role in verifying user identities and credentials. Its proactive approach, highlighted from 2024, helps safeguard Cloud Foundry against potential security risks and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security standards. Effective identity verification not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (35, 1138), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 03, 27))]\n\n## Cloud Integration and Interoperability\n\nThe Cloud Integration component ensures seamless integration and interoperability between various Cloud Foundry components and external services. Its focus on supporting adapters, such as Microsoft OneDrive, is crucial in maintaining Cloud Foundry's reputation and operational efficiency, especially in managing complex integrations and data exchange. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high standards of integration and interoperability. [Data: Sources (1137), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 27), (2025, 03, 27))]\n\n## Regional Availability and Scalability\n\nThe Regional Availability feature at Cloud Foundry ensures that services are accessible and scalable across various regions. Its focus on expanding availability, as seen in the addition of new data centers and regions, is crucial in maintaining Cloud Foundry's operational stability and scalability. Enhanced regional availability during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with customer needs and market demands. [Data: Sources (1136), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 27), (2025, 03, 27))]", "# SAP Technology and Finance Overview as of December 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology and finance, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2024.\n\n## Technology Operational Scope\n\nThe Technology Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2201, 2202), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 19))]\n\n## Finance and Credit Integration\n\nThe Finance Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the financial standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on credit integration, noted starting Q4 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex financial transactions and credit agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high financial standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (1710), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 01), (2024, 12, 19))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Technology and Finance Departments, established in Q4 2024, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are financially sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with financial compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (2203, 2204), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 01), (2024, 12, 19))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2024-09-30\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Cloud Services, focusing on key components, environments, and updates. It highlights the importance of these services in supporting business operations and technological advancements. The information is relevant to SAP Cloud Services as of 2024-09-30.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation\n\nSAP Build Process Automation is a key component of SAP Cloud Services, enabling the automation of business processes. The recent update to new regions, as of 2024-09-30, provides users with more flexibility and options for running enterprise accounts. This update is crucial for supporting business operations and technological advancements. [Data: Sources (585), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 30), (2024, 10, 08))]\n\n## SAP HANA Spatial Services Enhancements\n\nSAP HANA Spatial Services has undergone enhancements, including the implementation of Here Mapping V3 API, Here Routing V8 API, and Here Geocoding V7 API. These updates improve the mapping, routing, and geocoding capabilities of the service, supporting business operations and technological advancements. [Data: Source (2), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 30))]\n\n## Continuous Integration & Delivery Update\n\nThe Continuous Integration & Delivery service has been updated to switch the job execution backend from Microsoft Azure - US West (WA) to Amazon Web Services - US East (VA). This change does not affect the functionality or performance of the service, ensuring business continuity and operational stability. [Data: Source (3), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 27), (2024, 09, 27))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has undergone updates, including the change in behavior of target transformations that contain a combination of condition and skip operations for updates. This change ensures that users or groups are not deleted as they should be, supporting business operations and technological advancements. [Data: Sources (5, 6), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 25), (2024, 09, 25))]\n\n## Cloud Portal Service Updates\n\nCloud Portal Service has been updated to remove SAP SuccessFactors from the list of supported content providers. This change ensures that the service remains compliant with regulatory requirements and supports business operations. [Data: Source (7), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 23), (2025, 01, 23))]\n\n## Cloud Transport Management Updates\n\nCloud Transport Management has undergone updates, including the introduction of tags in SAP Cloud Transport Management. This change enables users to group transport nodes based on assigned tags, supporting business operations and technological advancements. [Data: Sources (8, 9), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 23), (2025, 01, 23))]\n\n## Destination Service Updates\n\nDestination Service has been updated to provide a previously generated and signed SAML assertion when fetching an OAuth2SAMLBearerAssertion destination. This change ensures that the service remains compliant with regulatory requirements and supports business operations. [Data: Source (10), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 23), (2025, 01, 23))]\n\n## Extensions Updates\n\nExtensions has undergone updates, including the introduction of a new formation type Integration with Joule. This change enables users to integrate SAP systems with Joule, supporting business operations and technological advancements. [Data: Sources (11, 12), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 23), (2025, 01, 23))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations as of 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has seen significant updates in 2024, including the introduction of new regions, event triggers, and in-app help for the action editor. These updates aim to improve user experience and streamline project management processes. The new regions feature allows for greater flexibility and scalability, while the event triggers enable users to automate tasks more efficiently. The in-app help feature provides users with easy access to information and support, reducing the need for external resources. These updates demonstrate SAP's commitment to innovation and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (2201, 3355), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 30))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has seen significant updates in 2024, including changes to the behavior of target transformations and the configuration of security questions and PIN codes for password recovery. These updates aim to improve the security and usability of the service. The changes to the behavior of target transformations ensure that users or groups that do not meet the condition are deleted as they should be. The configuration of security questions and PIN codes for password recovery now requires entering Edit mode, providing an additional layer of security. These updates demonstrate SAP's commitment to security and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (2205, 2206), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 30))]\n\n## ABAP Environment Updates\n\nABAP Environment has seen significant updates in 2024, including the introduction of new SAPUI5 version 1.120.8 and the use of hotfix collection 4. These updates aim to improve the performance and usability of the environment. The new SAPUI5 version provides a more modern and efficient user interface, while the use of hotfix collection 4 ensures that the environment is up-to-date and secure. These updates demonstrate SAP's commitment to innovation and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (3353, 3354), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 30))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP Cloud Foundry technology, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP BTP Cloud Foundry operations as of 2025.\n\n## Risk Management Operational Scope\n\nThe Risk Management Department at SAP BTP Cloud Foundry plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP BTP Cloud Foundry against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (790, 647), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 13), (2025, 07, 10))]\n\n## Legal Compliance and Governance\n\nThe Legal Compliance Department ensures that all SAP BTP Cloud Foundry operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP Cloud Foundry's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (588), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 16), (2025, 07, 10))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP BTP Cloud Foundry. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (765, 471), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 07, 10))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry Readiness Health Checks\n\nStarting at the end of September 2025, MTA deployment in Cloud Foundry will support Cloud Foundry readiness health checks by introducing new module-specific parameters. Users may encounter problems during MTA deployment if the parameters are already defined in their MTA descriptor but are incorrectly configured. In such case, the MTA deployments will start to fail with the error message: None of the instances of the app <app-name> become routable. Please verify that the defined MTA parameters for the readiness health check align with the app's code and configuration. [Data: Source (765), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 10), (2025, 09, 30))]\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack 2\n\nSAP Java Buildpack 2 now provides Apache TomEE 10, Plume distribution. SAP Java Buildpack 2 is now the default buildpack for Java applications. If you have TomEE-based applications that still run on SAP Java Buildpack 1, you can now start migrating them to SAP Java Buildpack 2. To learn how, see: Migrate your Applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2 [Data: Source (1348), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 07, 10))]\n\n## Root Certificate Replacement\n\nTo comply with the latest recommendations from the German BSI on the key-length for certificates and to ensure quantum-safe cryptography, SAP is switching to the DigiCert TLS RSA4096 Root G5 and “DigiCert Global Root G3” PKI in July 2025. For more information on this change and the schedule for individual SAP BTP regions, see SAP Note3566727. [Data: Source (1347), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 07, 10))]", "# SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Environment Overview as of June 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates as of June 2025. The information is relevant to the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment's operations and maintenance.\n\n## Upcoming Kubernetes 1.32 Release\n\nThe SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment is scheduled to be upgraded to the Kubernetes 1.32 release in the June 13-15th general maintenance windows. This upgrade will bring new features and improvements to the environment. The schedule for the upgrade is as follows: Asia Pacific & Japan (APJ) regions: 2025-06-14 14:00 - 17:00 UTC, Europe regions: 2025-06-14 21:00 - 24:00 UTC, Americas regions: 2025-06-15 06:00 - 09:00 UTC, and Middle East regions: 2025-06-13 17:00 - 21:00 UTC. [Data: Sources (790), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 13), (2025, 06, 15))]\n\n## Removal of SAP Java Buildpack 1\n\nSAP Java Buildpack 1 has been deprecated and will be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment on June 30, 2025. This removal will affect deployments of MTAs containing modules of type java, java.tomcat, and java.tomee. To ensure compliance with this change, the MTA deployment will switch the default value for the buildpack parameter from sap_java_buildpack (SAP Java Buildpack 1) to sap_java_buildpack_jakarta (SAP Java Buildpack 2) starting from the beginning of July. [Data: Sources (649, 870), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 30), (2025, 07, 01))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry API v2 Deprecation and Removal\n\nThe Cloud Foundry API v2 is deprecated and will be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment in the first quarter of 2026. The usage of the Cloud Foundry API v2 is restricted by rate limits, which will decrease over time and eventually reach zero in the first quarter of 2026. To ensure compliance with this change, users must migrate any direct usage of CF API v2 to CF API v3. [Data: Sources (871), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2026, 01, 01))]\n\n## Root Certificate Replacement in the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nThe root certificate authority (CA) used to issue the certificates on SAP domains for the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment needs to be changed. The old CA 'DigiCert Global Root CA G2' (G2) will be replaced by the newer 'DigiCert TLS RSA4096 Root G5' (G5). Clients of applications offered by SAP and of those operated by customers must add the new CA certificate to their trust store in order to ensure a seamless transition. [Data: Sources (872), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 18), (2025, 06, 30))]\n\n## Dynamic Expression Playground\n\nThe Expression Playground of SAP Automation Pilot is now available to test and debug dynamic expressions before using them in commands. The playground also gives users the option to load commands that are prepopulated with sample values, which allows them to test how the expressions will function during execution. [Data: Sources (873), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 06, 30))]\n\n## Loading of Existing Configuration during Instance Update\n\nCloud Logging enables loading of existing configuration during instance update via cockpit. Please note that if the last update performed only includes partial parameters, the loading configurations will only bring the last updated partial parameters. [Data: Sources (874), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 06, 30))]\n\n## Support for Monitoring Security Recommendations\n\nCloud Logging service now supports Monitoring Security Recommendations with SAP Cloud ALM. Please also note SAP BTP Security Recommendations (for SAP Cloud Logging Service). [Data: Sources (875), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 06, 30))]\n\n## SAP Fiori Horizon theme\n\nThe user interface of Feature Flags Dashboard is now upgraded to SAP Fiori, Horizon. For more information about this theme, see blog post: SAP Fiori Evolution: Horizon Now Generally Available in UI Technologies. [Data: Sources (876), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 06, 30))]\n\n## Service Instance Sharing\n\nYou can now share SAP Feature Flags service instances between different Cloud Foundry organizations in the same subaccount. [Data: Sources (877), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 06, 30))]", "# SAP BTP and SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud Update Overview\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and changes in SAP BTP and SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud, highlighting the importance of these updates in maintaining the stability and functionality of the systems. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP BTP Update Overview\n\nSAP BTP has undergone several updates and changes, including the deprecation of weak client certificate chains, the introduction of new features such as built-in support and the April release of the SAP Cloud Application Programming Model. These updates aim to improve the security and functionality of the system, ensuring continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective updates not only prevent system anomalies but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 01), (2024, 10, 22))]\n\n## SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud Update Overview\n\nSAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud has also undergone several updates and changes, including the integration with new credit agencies, the introduction of new features such as extracted line items and improved machine learning models. These updates aim to improve the functionality and efficiency of the system, ensuring continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective updates not only prevent system anomalies but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (3, 4), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 01), (2024, 10, 22))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the SAP BTP and SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud teams, established in 2023, ensures that system updates are aligned with regulatory requirements and that compliance measures consider system risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating system updates with compliance strategies at the company. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (5, 6), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 01), (2024, 10, 22))]", "# SAP Technology Updates as of June 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of key SAP technology updates, focusing on components such as Content Agent Service, SAP Build Process Automation, SAP Document AI, SAP Dynamic Forms, API Management, Kyma Runtime, SAP Cloud Application Event Hub, SAP Alert Notification Service, Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry, and Cloud Logging. The information highlights the importance of these updates in maintaining SAP's technological integrity and operational stability.\n\n## Content Agent Service and SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nThe Content Agent Service and SAP Build Process Automation components have undergone significant updates, enabling improved content management and process automation. These updates are crucial for maintaining SAP's content management and process automation capabilities, ensuring seamless integration and operational efficiency. [Data: Sources (789, 790), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 16), (2025, 06, 24))]\n\n## SAP Document AI and SAP Dynamic Forms Enhancements\n\nThe SAP Document AI and SAP Dynamic Forms components have been enhanced, providing improved document analysis and form management capabilities. These updates are essential for maintaining SAP's document analysis and form management capabilities, ensuring accurate and efficient document processing and form management. [Data: Sources (790, 791), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 16), (2025, 06, 27))]\n\n## API Management and Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe API Management and Kyma Runtime components have been updated, enabling improved API management and Kubernetes runtime capabilities. These updates are critical for maintaining SAP's API management and Kubernetes runtime capabilities, ensuring secure and efficient API management and Kubernetes deployment. [Data: Sources (790, 792), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 13), (2025, 06, 15))]\n\n## SAP Cloud Application Event Hub and SAP Alert Notification Service Updates\n\nThe SAP Cloud Application Event Hub and SAP Alert Notification Service components have been updated, providing improved event monitoring and notification capabilities. These updates are essential for maintaining SAP's event monitoring and notification capabilities, ensuring timely and accurate event monitoring and notification. [Data: Sources (793, 794), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 12), (2025, 06, 13))]\n\n## Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry and Cloud Logging Updates\n\nThe Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry and Cloud Logging components have been updated, enabling improved application deployment and logging capabilities. These updates are critical for maintaining SAP's application deployment and logging capabilities, ensuring secure and efficient application deployment and logging. [Data: Sources (795, 796), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 12), (2025, 06, 12))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_e698c30fa83ffb57ec4d7943773d648f30bb5ddb0c0dd2d3e88dc3c6e1430fe3_v2"}